{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" validate --help; python3 - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,os\nx=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT']))\nprint(json.dumps(x,indent=2)[:6000])\nfor f in ['results/summary.json','results/fwe_clusters.csv']:\n print('\\\\n---',f); print(open(f).read()[:3500])\nPY\n\"","aggregated_output":".bashrc sourced.\n.bash_profile sourced\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py [-h]\n                          {items,validate,encode,decode,template,set,stamp,table} ...\n\nSTAMPED checklist responses: read the items, validate, encode, decode.\n\nThe vendored checklist in ``../checklist/`` is the only item source, and this\nscript is the only writer of a checklist-app URL.  See\n``../references/response-format.md`` for the response JSON and\n``../references/verdicts.md`` for the statuses.\n\nSubcommands\n-----------\nitems      list the pinned items (id, level, principle codes, text)\nset        answer one item in a response JSON, in place (what every run was\n           otherwise writing a merge script for)\ntable      the per-item markdown table response-format.md section 4 asks for\nstamp      fill harness, model, scope and kind; optionally hash a retained capture\nvalidate   check a response JSON against the pin and the app's constraints\nencode     response JSON -> checklist-app URL\ndecode     checklist-app URL -> response JSON (how a filled web form becomes\n           reference answers for calibration)\ntemplate   emit a response JSON skeleton with every item not-checked\n\nExit codes: 0 ok, 1 validation failed, 2 usage.\n\npositional arguments:\n  {items,validate,encode,decode,template,set,stamp,table}\n    items               list the pinned items\n    validate            check a response JSON\n    encode              response JSON -> URL\n    decode              URL -> response JSON\n    template            emit an all-not-checked response JSON\n    set                 answer one item in a response JSON, in place\n    stamp               fill harness, model, scope, kind and capture identity\n    table               print the per-item markdown table\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py validate [-h] response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n{\n  \"capture\": {\n    \"sha256\": \"73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b\",\n    \"uri\": \"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/runs/narps-neutral-r1-09/attempt-01/native/original-delivery/manifest.json\"\n  },\n  \"capture_finished_at\": \"2026-10-16T07:05:36.714511+00:00\",\n  \"capture_status\": \"complete\",\n  \"captured_at\": \"2026-10-16T07:05:36.347041+00:00\",\n  \"errors\": [],\n  \"head_commit\": \"ad3956ae64dcbdd1eec6af4ed21e0b168e478106\",\n  \"kind\": \"worker-end-state\",\n  \"omissions\": [],\n  \"schema_version\": 2,\n  \"seed_identities\": {\n    \"common_prompt_sha256\": \"cb2431489d8f92c6737bb07017c88a24a784ae51fd15d655a122d9938d96429b\",\n    \"common_resources_sha256\": \"3be6e7238a5e9bd21d73df44d3dcbb7636999e13334626f544ae676f42bb91b7\",\n    \"inputs\": [\n      {\n        \"annex_key\": \"MD5E-s1794522--2a6f64556ba73c42049c33979409bb66.nii.gz\",\n        \"bytes\": 1794522,\n        \"git_blob\": \"7fe8af426107cd5cf96caba75335f818f4b6e370\",\n        \"mode\": \"120000\",\n        \"path\": \"input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\",\n        \"sha256\": \"baf3440fbc7f5f59dea28d231e9c5eb9cf00a15b6924342f4b79e7faf56a929a\",\n        \"source_mode\": \"120000\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"annex_key\": \"MD5E-s1762018--87ead2a2104507d24085d3136b907ea3.nii.