{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"ls -lh report.md scripts/group_analysis.py notebooks/narps_gain_group_analysis.ipynb results figures input; sed -n '1,100p' input/study-task.md; sed -n '1,180p' input/sources.json; git status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all\"","aggregated_output":".bashrc sourced.\n.bash_profile sourced\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff   4.8K Oct 16 06:40 notebooks/narps_gain_group_analysis.ipynb\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff   5.3K Oct 16 06:40 report.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff   8.3K Oct 16 06:40 scripts/group_analysis.py\n\nfigures:\ntotal 744\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff    49K Oct 16 06:40 posterior_fwe_cluster.png\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff    66K Oct 16 06:40 vmpfc_participant_effects.png\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff    52K Oct 16 06:40 whole_brain_fwe_and_vmpfc.png\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff   199K Oct 16 06:40 whole_brain_fwe_glassbrain.png\n\ninput:\ntotal 64\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 56 johnlee  staff   1.8K Oct 16 06:40 data\n-rw-r--r--@  1 johnlee  staff   1.7K Oct 16 06:40 participants.tsv\n-rw-r--r--@  1 johnlee  staff    19K Oct 16 06:40 sources.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 johnlee  staff   1.4K Oct 16 06:40 study-task.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 johnlee  staff   1.3K Oct 16 06:40 upstream-methods.md\n\nresults:\ntotal 2376\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff   341B Oct 16 06:40 fwe_clusters.csv\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff    31K Oct 16 06:40 group_t_fwe05_positive.nii.gz\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff   1.0M Oct 16 06:40 group_t_unthresholded.nii.gz\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff    75K Oct 16 06:40 p_fwe_signflip_maxT.nii.gz\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff   6.4K Oct 16 06:40 summary.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 johnlee  staff   1.6K Oct 16 06:40 vmPFC_subject_means.csv\n# Potential gains and brain activity\n\nDoes increasing potential monetary gain produce a greater fMRI response in the ventromedial prefrontal cortex (vmPFC) in the NARPS equal-indifference group?\n\nTest the hypothesis that this response increases with potential gain.\nParticipants performed a mixed-gambles task, deciding whether to accept gambles with possible gains and losses.\nIn this group, the range of potential gains was twice the range of potential losses.\n\nInvestigate the question at the group-analysis stage using the supplied 54 participant gain-effect maps and metadata.\nPreprocessing and individual modeling are fixed inputs, described in `upstream-methods.md`; do not repeat them or download time-series scans.\nChoose scientifically defensible group models, quality checks, software and visualizations.\nAccount for what the supplied effect estimates measure and the limits of their upstream model.\nUse whole-brain correction for multiple comparisons when evaluating support for the hypothesis, as required by the original study; justify how you identify vmPFC.\n\nProduce a concise scientific report with informative figures and the code and results supporting your conclusions.\nExplain uncertainty, exclusions and limitations, including what a lack of support would mean.\nPrior teams' answers are not ground truth or a required result.\n\nSource: [NARPS original analysis instructions, Hypothesis 1](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf).\n{\n  \"study\": \"NARPS Hypothesis 1: group inference from fixed participant effects\",\n  \"collection\": \"https://neurovault.org/collections/4932/\",\n  \"team\": \"AO86\",\n  \"image_metadata_api\": \"https://neurovault.org/api/collections/4932/images/?limit=2000\",\n  \"selection\": \"All single-subject unthresholded hypo1 cope images; participant IDs exactly match the 54 equalIndifference participants in the pinned source table.\",\n  \"maps\": 54,\n  \"map_bytes\": 96387264,\n  \"map_type\": \"participant contrast parameter estimate, not a z/t statistic or a group result\",\n  \"spatial_reference\": \"MNI152NLin2009cAsym\",\n  \"upstream_processing_fixed\": true,\n  \"cohort_source\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OpenNeuroDatasets/ds001734/64ec117560ab58ed0fe1273f3e90887b1768b268/participants.tsv\",\n    \"git_commit\": \"64ec117560ab58ed0fe1273f3e90887b1768b268\",\n    \"sha256\": \"d127d700f9a519338da295ea56455bf7bb46ca572f726da72ef7b57c310687b8\",\n    \"transformation\": \"Select group == equalIndifference; preserve all columns and values.\"\n  },\n  \"methods_source\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/poldrack/narps/0a9d71a5ab435b40dcd50fea82d2961a43f0a3fc/ImageAnalyses/metadata_files/analysis_pipelines_for_analysis.xlsx\",\n    \"git_commit\": \"0a9d71a5ab435b40dcd50fea82d2961a43f0a3fc\",\n    \"sha256\": \"bfb66119c6beb26e5d3fc84638435cf6c49b40e5eb06606bfecaee0aa48d82b7\",\n    \"sheet\": \"Sheet1\",\n    \"header_excel_row\": 2,\n    \"team_id\": \"AO86\"\n  },\n  \"checksum_scope\": \"SHA256 values are computed from retrieved bytes; NeuroVault metadata independently supplies file sizes but no source checksums.\",\n  \"files\": {\n    \"data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\": {\n      \"url\": \"https://neurovault.org/media/images/4932/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\",\n      \"image_id\": 118651,\n      \"participant_id\": \"sub-001\",\n      \"bytes\": 1794522,\n      \"sha256\": \"baf3440fbc7f5f59dea28d231e9c5eb9cf00a15b6924342f4b79e7faf56a929a\",\n      \"transformation\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"data/sub-003_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\": {\n      \"url\": \"https://neurovault.org/media/images/4932/sub-003_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\",\n      \"image_id\": 118661,\n      \"participant_id\": \"sub-003\",\n      \"bytes\": 1762018,\n      \"sha256\": \"a8c9b6276d1597bc43695516c9ac5b2893a8d8408cd053161ceaddbd42dafb20\",\n      \"transformation\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"data/sub-005_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\": {\n      \"url\": \"https://neurovault.org/media/images/4932/sub-005_hypo1_cope.nii.gz\",\n      \"image_id\": 118671,\n      \"participant_id\": \"sub-005\",\n      \"bytes\": 1847315,\n      \"sha256\": \"415383874c65fd9e10bb03bf2aa59b