{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"I found an inspection mistake: the NeuroVault `curl` command ran with the operational workspace as its working directory, so its captured stdout and stderr were written there. I will leave those files in place as required, preserve copies and hashes in the assessment directory, and report this as an assessor-created integrity mismatch. The science files had already been read before that check; the access result will be treated only as a host response, not worker evidence."}}
