{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"cat item-table.md >> 2026-10-16-assessment.md\ncat >> 2026-10-16-assessment.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Flagged items\n\n- **must/004:** \"'`tree-clean` treated any uncommitted analysis content as the whole versioning answer; the stop inventory shows Git use, but the scientific deliverables were untracked, so `partial` is retained.\n- **must/007, must/008:** `entry-point` missed the report/notebook route. The notebook runs the analysis script, but setup instructions remain incomplete.\n- **must/011, must/012:** `platform-assumptions` scans commands only; the report lists packages but leaves system and install requirements undocumented.\n- **should/002:** `ci-present` found no recognized CI; complete delivered evidence also has no recurring test record, so the finding is `unmet`.\n- **must/014 and should/008:** These checklist items duplicate the same question and therefore share the same answer (`upstream-duplicate`).\n\n## Not checked\n\n- **should/004:** No fresh replay was attempted because no worker-supplied environment specification or installation route makes environment reconstruction possible. A supplied, pinned dependency declaration and fresh-host replay would settle it. See [replay record](replay-record.json).\n\n## Goals and kind\n\nThe supplied task asks for a group-level answer using the 54 fixed AO86 gain-effect maps, with whole-brain correction, interpretable vmPFC localization, code, outputs, figures and limitations. I assume this documented goal because no human guidance was attached. The primary kind is a **study**, so this review emphasizes complete inputs and the link from code/actions/environment to results.\n\n## Additional finding outside the checklist\n\nThe captured tree has no reuse/license statement for worker-produced code and results (`extra_items` in `response.json`; the `license-declared` probe). No license terms are inferred from public availability of the input collection.\n\n## Checklist and provenance\n\nChecklist link: [open this response in the STAMPED checklist app](2026-10-16-url.txt). The complete machine-readable judgments and evidence are in [response.json](response.json); scripted probe output is [probes.json](probes.json).\n\nProduced by `assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles` 0.1.0 with `stamped-conventions` 0.1.0, checklist 0.3.1 (`stamped-checklist-schema@v0.3.1`, `af259ba`), on the original capture `73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b`, original HEAD `ad3956ae64dcbdd1eec6af4ed21e0b168e478106`, 2026-10-16, Codex API / gpt-6.1-sol. The frozen runner check used source commit `9852d8360f9519d21d11099b45f5deb8ba80cb28` and environment commit `3552d5003a2485b6405805236d5c54e7ed42f097`. Probe output: `probes.json`.\nEOF\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"cat item-table.md >> 2026-10-16-assessment.md\ncat >> 2026-10-16-assessment.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Flagged items\n\n- **must/004:** \"'`tree-clean` treated any uncommitted analysis content as the whole versioning answer; the stop inventory shows Git use, but the scientific deliverables were untracked, so `partial` is retained.\n- **must/007, must/008:** `entry-point` missed the report/notebook route. The notebook runs the analysis script, but setup instructions remain incomplete.\n- **must/011, must/012:** `platform-assumptions` scans commands only; the report lists packages but leaves system and install requirements undocumented.\n- **should/002:** `ci-present` found no recognized CI; complete delivered evidence also has no recurring test record, so the finding is `unmet`.\n- **must/014 and should/008:** These checklist items duplicate the same question and therefore share the same answer (`upstream-duplicate`).\n\n## Not checked\n\n- **should/004:** No fresh replay was attempted because no worker-supplied environment specification or installation route makes environment reconstruction possible. A supplied, pinned dependency declaration and fresh-host replay would settle it. See [replay record](replay-record.json).\n\n## Goals and kind\n\nThe supplied task asks for a group-level answer using the 54 fixed AO86 gain-effect maps, with whole-brain correction, interpretable vmPFC localization, code, outputs, figures and limitations. I assume this documented goal because no human guidance was attached. The primary kind is a **study**, so this review emphasizes complete inputs and the link from code/actions/environment to results.\n\n## Additional finding outside the checklist\n\nThe captured tree has no reuse/license statement for worker-produced code and results (`extra_items` in `response.json`; the `license-declared` probe). No license terms are inferred from public availability of the input collection.\n\n## Checklist and provenance\n\nChecklist link: [open this response in the STAMPED checklist app](2026-10-16-url.txt). The complete machine-readable judgments and evidence are in [response.json](response.json); scripted probe output is [probes.json](probes.json).\n\nProduced by `assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles` 0.1.0 with `stamped-conventions` 0.1.0, checklist 0.3.1 (`stamped-checklist-schema@v0.3.1`, `af259ba`), on the original capture `73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b`, original HEAD `ad3956ae64dcbdd1eec6af4ed21e0b168e478106`, 2026-10-16, Codex API / gpt-6.1-sol. The frozen runner check used source commit `9852d8360f9519d21d11099b45f5deb8ba80cb28` and environment commit `3552d5003a2485b6405805236d5c54e7ed42f097`. Probe output: `probes.json`.\nEOF\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response encode response.json > 2026-10-16-url.txt\nnl -ba 2026-10-16-assessment.md | sed -n '\"'24,44p'; sed -n '1,12p' item-table.md; tail -n 6 2026-10-16-url.txt; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nx=json.load(open('response.json'))\nfrom collections import Counter\nfor k in ('must','should','may'):\n vals=[v['status'] for key,v in x['responses'].items() if key.split(':')[1].startswith(k+'/')]\n print(k,Counter(vals))\nprint('capture',x['object'].get('capture'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response encode response.json > 2026-10-16-url.txt\nnl -ba 2026-10-16-assessment.md | sed -n '\"'24,44p'; sed -n '1,12p' item-table.md; tail -n 6 2026-10-16-url.txt; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nx=json.load(open('response.json'))\nfrom collections import Counter\nfor k in ('must','should','may'):\n vals=[v['status'] for key,v in x['responses'].items() if key.split(':')[1].startswith(k+'/')]\n print(k,Counter(vals))\nprint('capture',x['object'].get('capture'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"✔ The default environment has been installed.\n    24\t## Scientific assessment\n    25\t\n    26\t**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The reported conclusion is: “No whole-brain-corrected evidence supports a positive gain effect in vmPFC in the NARPS equal-indifference group.” The analysis tests 54 independent participant effects with a positive one-sample statistic and a sign-flip maximum-t correction across 210,968 voxels. It reports 24 corrected voxels in three posterior clusters, and none in its explicit broad vmPFC locator; the locator mean is −0.003 (95% t interval −0.021 to 0.016), with its most positive voxel at max-statistic FWE p=.938 (`content/workspace/results/summary.json`, `content/workspace/results/fwe_clusters.csv`, `content/workspace/report.md`). This supports the bounded absence-of-evidence conclusion, not a claim that the true vmPFC response is zero.\n    27\t\n    28\tThe analysis is scientifically defensible for the supplied fixed inputs: it checks image geometry and data quality, keeps all 54 intended participants, and corrects the directional whole-brain search. The nonzero-in-at-least-90%-of-maps coverage mask is an explicit but data-dependent coverage choice; inference is conditional on that tested mask. Sign-flip validity assumes symmetric participant effects under the null, and absent first-level variance maps prevent precision weighting. The upstream gain coefficient reflects a normalized regressor conditional on AO86's fixed model, not BOLD change per currency unit. The broad MNI coordinate box is a transparent anatomical approximation rather than an independently defined anatomical mask. The report acknowledges these constraints and does not overstate the null result.\n    29\t\n    30\tThe separately reported hypothesis outcome is **no whole-brain-corrected support for a positive vmPFC gain effect**. It is not inferred from the adequacy category.\n    31\t\n    32\t## Replay and access\n    33\t\n    34\tReplay was **not checked**. The notebook's documented route runs `scripts/group_analysis.py`, and the script's ten generated artifacts are explicitly listed in `replay-record.json`. However, the worker supplied package versions only in prose and no environment declaration or install instructions; I did not substitute the assessor environment. No replay attempt was made. The record declares inputs/source protected, output selection, and the intended numeric comparison rule.\n    35\t\n    36\tThe intended recipient is a researcher using the worker-declared route. `report.md` and `input/sources.json` point to NeuroVault collection 4932 and the 54 map URLs. The assessment host received HTTP/2 200 from the collection endpoint; this tests only that host/endpoint, not all map payloads or access terms. The worker declared no route for the report, script, notebook, figures or results. Coordinator delivery is not worker publication evidence. Details and captured command output are in `access-record.json` and `access-route.*`.\n    37\t\n    38\t## Capture integrity and attribution\n    39\t\n    40\tThe frozen probes ran against the operational copy and wrote only assessment-side `probes.json` and `response.json`; they are assessor measurements, not worker evidence. The NeuroVault request output is also preserved in the assessment directory. No additional target changes were observed in Git status; final exact integrity is left to the launcher verification. The permitted annex keys database files are excluded from worker attribution if inspection touched them; logical database equivalence is not claimed.\n    41\t\n    42\tThe stop receipt identifies the worker stop at the original HEAD and reports a complete capture with no omissions. Git status shows `report.md`, `scripts/`, `notebooks/`, `results/`, `figures/` and `.codex/` as untracked at that state. The input maps are annex-backed. Later coordinator preservation does not earn worker tracking, publication or reproducibility credit. The capture contains `.codex` and `.entire` material that may expose assistance context; it was not used to grade scientific or STAMPED attainment, and no treatment assignment was inferred or reported.\n    43\t\n    44\t## Per-item judgments\n| item | principles | status | source | evidence | reason |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| must/001 | S.1 | met | judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/input/sources.json` | The full study, inputs, code, and outputs share the captured workspace root. |\n| must/002 | S.1 | met | judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz`, `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/input/sources.json` | All 54 input pointers resolve to annex objects inside this captured root. |\n| must/003 | S.1 | unmet | judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/scripts/group_analysis.py`, `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/report.md` | No delivered environment includes or links the required scientific packages. |\n| must/004 | T.1,T.3,T.5 | partial ⚠ (a MUST is not satisfied by partial) | probe:tree-clean+judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/scripts/group_analysis.py`, `probes.json` | Git is used, but the scientific code, report, notebook, figures and results were untracked at worker stop. |\n| must/005 | T.1,T.3,T.5 | met | probe:large-in-annex | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz` | Git-annex stores all 54 participant maps as large binary inputs. |\n| must/006 | T.1,T.3,T.5 | unmet | probe:run-env-linked+judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/results/summary.json`, `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/report.md` | The result summary records inputs and seed, but no exact environment or run record links actions to it. |\n| must/007 | A.1 | partial ⚠ (a MUST is not satisfied by partial) | probe:entry-point+judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/report.md`, `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/notebooks/narps_gain_group_analysis.ipynb` | Report and notebook explain the analysis route, but give no dependency installation instructions. |\n| must/008 | A.1 | met | probe:entry-point+judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/notebooks/narps_gain_group_analysis.ipynb` | The notebook identifies and runs the authoritative group-analysis script. |\n| must/009 | P.1 | met | probe:no-abs-paths+judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/scripts/group_analysis.py` | The analysis script resolves inputs and outputs relative to its own workspace root. |\n| must/010 | P.1 | unmet | probe:env-spec-tracked+judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/scripts/group_analysis.py`, `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/report.md` | Required Python packages have no dependency declaration or reproducible installer. |\nhttps://checklist.stamped-principles.org/?checklist=0.3.1&responses_version=0.3.1&cols=auto&sections=off&format=3&%3D\nmust Counter({'unmet': 8, 'met': 5, 'partial': 4})\nshould Counter({'unmet': 5, 'met': 1, 'partial': 1, 'not-applicable': 1, 'not-checked': 1})\nmay Counter({'met': 4, 'partial': 1})\ncapture {'uri': '/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-09-j01/canonical/manifest.json', 'sha256': '73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
