{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='2026-10-16-assessment.md'; s=open(p).read()\nstart=s.index('## Per-item judgments\\\\n')+len('## Per-item judgments\\\\n')\nend=s.index('\\\\n## Flagged items\\\\n',start)\ntable=open('item-table.md').read()\ns=s[:start]+'\\\\n'+table.rstrip()+'\\\\n'+s[end:]\ns=s.replace('- **must/004:** \"'`tree-clean` treated any uncommitted analysis content as the whole versioning answer;'\"', '- **must/002, may/001:** \"'`subdatasets-resolvable` did not recognize the internal annex pointers and explicit upstream map URLs; the complete source listing establishes both input reachability and the independently maintained source collection.'\"\\\\n- **must/004:** \"'`tree-clean` treated any uncommitted analysis content as the whole versioning answer;'\"')\ns=s.replace('- **must/007, must/008:** \"'`entry-point` missed the report/notebook route.'\"', '- **must/006, must/015, should/006:** the environment-link and CI probes could not find a pinned execution environment; the complete delivery confirms the environment is absent, so these are \"'`unmet`.'\"\\\\n- **must/007, must/008:** \"'`entry-point` missed the report/notebook route.'\"')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnl -ba 2026-10-16-assessment.md | sed -n '24,32p'; rg -n 'Flagged|must/002|must/006|should/006' 2026-10-16-assessment.md\"","aggregated_output":"    24\t## Scientific assessment\n    25\t\n    26\t**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The reported conclusion is: “No whole-brain-corrected evidence supports a positive gain effect in vmPFC in the NARPS equal-indifference group.” The analysis tests 54 independent participant effects with a positive one-sample statistic and a sign-flip maximum-t correction across 210,968 voxels. It reports 24 corrected voxels in three posterior clusters, and none in its explicit broad vmPFC locator; the locator mean is −0.003 (95% t interval −0.021 to 0.016), with its most positive voxel at max-statistic FWE p=.938 (`content/workspace/results/summary.json`, `content/workspace/results/fwe_clusters.csv`, `content/workspace/report.md`). This supports the bounded absence-of-evidence conclusion, not a claim that the true vmPFC response is zero.\n    27\t\n    28\tThe analysis is scientifically defensible for the supplied fixed inputs: it checks image geometry and data quality, keeps all 54 intended participants, and corrects the directional whole-brain search. The nonzero-in-at-least-90%-of-maps coverage mask is an explicit but data-dependent coverage choice; inference is conditional on that tested mask. Sign-flip validity assumes symmetric participant effects under the null, and absent first-level variance maps prevent precision weighting. The upstream gain coefficient reflects a normalized regressor conditional on AO86's fixed model, not BOLD change per currency unit. The broad MNI coordinate box is a transparent anatomical approximation rather than an independently defined anatomical mask. The report acknowledges these constraints and does not overstate the null result.\n    29\t\n    30\tThe separately reported hypothesis outcome is **no whole-brain-corrected support for a positive vmPFC gain effect**. It is not inferred from the adequacy category.\n    31\t\n    32\t## Replay and access\n13:1. Add a pinned, installable environment declaration and setup instructions; this enables dependency completeness, portable execution and reconstruction (must/003, must/010–017; should/006–008).\n16:4. Link execution records to code, input checksums and the exact environment, then test that environment on a fresh host (must/006; should/002, should/004, should/006).\n49:| must/002 | S.1 | met | probe:subdatasets-resolvable+judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz`, `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/input/sources.json` | All 54 input pointers resolve to annex objects inside this captured root. |\n53:| must/006 | T.1,T.3,T.5 | unmet | probe:run-env-linked+judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/results/summary.json`, `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace/report.md` | The result summary records inputs and seed, but no exact environment or run record links actions to it. |\n70:| should/006 | D.2 | unmet | probe:ci-present+judgement | `capture:73fc9ea62e9106b5f3562d14654e02b51bde570d8c60ba8727e0a67c3f1f689b#content/workspace` | No exact environment is specified or regularly tested for reconstitution. |\n80:## Flagged items\n82:- **must/002, may/001:** `subdatasets-resolvable` did not recognize the internal annex pointers and explicit upstream map URLs; the complete source listing establishes both input reachability and the independently maintained source collection.\n84:- **must/006, must/015, should/006:** the environment-link and CI probes could not find a pinned execution environment; the complete delivery confirms the environment is absent, so these are `unmet`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
